es></name><name><surname>Roth</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>MacQueen</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Communication in the hospital setting: a survey of medical and everyday language use amongst patients, nurses and doctors</article-title><source>Soc Sci Med</source><year>1989</year><volume>28</volume><fpage>339</fpage><lpage>46</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2705006</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b10"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Boyd</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Citro</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Cardiac patient education literature: can patients read what we give them?</article-title><source>J Cardiac Rehab</source><year>1983</year><volume>3</volume><fpage>513</fpage><lpage>6</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b11"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Braddock</surname><given-names>CH</given-names><suffix>III</suffix></name><name><surname>Fihn</surname><given-names>SD</given-names></name><name><surname>Levinson</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>How doctors and patients discuss routine clinical decisions. Informed decision making in the outpatient setting</article-title><source>J Gen Intern Med</source><year>1997</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>339</fpage><lpage>45</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9192250</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b12"><citation citation-type="journal"><collab>Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC)</collab><article-title>Decline in deaths from heart disease and stroke&#x02013;United States, 1900&#x02013;1999</article-title><source>MMWR Morb Mortal Wkly Rep</source><year>1999</year><volume>48</volume><fpage>649</fpage><lpage>56</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10488780</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b13"><citation citatio