ian</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Williams</surname><given-names>MV</given-names></name><name><surname>Peel</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Health literacy and knowledge of chronic disease</article-title><source>Patient Educ Counsel</source><year>2003</year><volume>51</volume><fpage>267</fpage><lpage>75</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Golbeck</surname><given-names>AL</given-names></name><name><surname>Ahlers-Schmidt</surname><given-names>CR</given-names></name><name><surname>Paschal</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>A definition and operational framework for health numeracy</article-title><source>Am J Prev Med</source><year>2005</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>375</fpage><lpage>6</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16242604</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b22"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Grady</surname><given-names>KL</given-names></name><name><surname>Dracup</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Kennedy</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Team management of patients with heart failure: A statement for healthcare professionals from The Cardiovascular Nursing Council of the American Heart Association</article-title><source>Circulation</source><year>2000</year><volume>102</volume><fpage>2443</fpage><lpage>56</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11067802</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b23"><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Hauser</surname><given-names>RM</given-names></name><name><surname>Edley</surname><given-names>CF</given-names></name><name><surname>Koenig</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><source>Measuring literacy: performance levels 